  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-IP24-SWZ801</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The employers&apos; organization need ongoing technical capacity support to facilitate their effective engagement in national policy and legislative reform initiatives and to maintain strategic influence in ongoing national dialogue for policy reform. Operators and informal businesses in the informal economy lack adequate voice and representation at platforms for national social dialogue and policy engagement that would allow them to push strong advocacy for the betterment of their working conditions.  Violence and harassment in the world of work remains a challenge employers confront that impacts negatively on worker productivity necessitating the need for more focused and impactful interventions.  The reality of climate change and the need for impactful interventions to mitigate against harmful business practices to the environment have necessitated that businesses operate responsibly and contribute to a sustainable future by reducing their carbon footprint. 
The strategy focuses on capacity support to the employers&#x2019; organizations to engage meaningfully in legislative and policy reform through training support on provisions of legislation and policy, as well as on provisions International Labour Standards underpinning such policies; capacity support to employers&#x2019; organizations to extend improved services to their members, including those representing small and informal business entities; training support to employers organizations to roll-out support to their members to combat violence and harassment at work; and training and capacity support to employers organizations to comply with Environmental, Social and Governance (ESG) requirements.</narrative>
  </description>
